diff --git a/before/specs/roadmap/staged-training.md b/after/specs/roadmap/staged-training.md
index 8b57eb2..664af24 100644
--- a/before/specs/roadmap/staged-training.md
+++ b/after/specs/roadmap/staged-training.md
@@ -202,3 +202,52 @@ sibling branches. Full-model templates are cloned through the binary inference f
 internally, while checkpoint and inference JSON formats remain backward compatible.
 Tests compare branch predictions/recipes and checkpoint round trips after independent
 pruning, banding, smoothing and path reconfiguration.
+
+# Restore and fingerprint costs
+
+Staged workflows restore models and check data identity many times per path. Neither may
+cost more than the information it needs.
+
+**Model restore.** Estimator `from_bytes` / `from_json` reads the native objective, axis
+provenance, feature names and document kind through native accessors:
+- `objective()` returns `(loss, tweedie_rho)`;
+- `provenance()` returns `(raw id, categorical TS encoding or None)` for each axis;
+- `feature_names` is the existing getter;
+- `_native_json_kind(text)` reads a native document's top-level `kind` through a native
+  probe, without building Python objects. Its answers and errors are exactly those of
+  `json.loads(text).get("kind")`: non-objects have no kind, and a repeated key keeps its
+  last value. Documents the probe cannot parse (NaN or Infinity literals, very deep nesting,
+  malformed text) use Python's parser, so they keep its answers and `JSONDecodeError`.
+
+They do not serialise the native model to JSON and parse it back in Python. Each accessor
+reports exactly the values `to_json()` reports. In particular, `tweedie_rho` keeps the
+same decimal rendering of the stored `f32`, so restored estimator parameters, and every
+result computed from them, are unchanged. A load determines the document kind once.
+`deployed_census` also reports the count of factored tables, so path-point complexity
+diagnostics never serialise a bank. Wire formats are unchanged.
+
+**Immutable training state.**
+- The full-fit training state computes its data digest once: at capture for a fresh fit,
+  or from the manifest digest that load has already verified.
+- `session.data_digest` returns that stored value. Forks share it.
+- The state's owned numeric arrays (rows, target, weight, exposure, groups) are read-only;
+  writing to them raises. Categorical values are an owned deep copy that no session operation
+  mutates. They become read-only codes when the checkpoint stores categorical columns as codes
+  plus levels; until then the cached digest relies on that ownership.
+- The unit weight vector of an unweighted fit is built once.
+- Internal checks of the raw feature count use the validated state, not a model rebuild.
+- `full_model` and `model()` still return independent estimators.
+- Once restore is cheap, re-measure the remaining internal `full_model` uses. Introduce a
+  shared template only if they still matter.
+
+**Path families.** `candidate_bytes` serialises only the requested point's metadata.
+`points` keeps returning detached copies.
+
+**Tests:**
+- restored estimators have attributes equal to today's for every envelope fixture
+  (regressor, classifier, multiclass, tables, legacy bare blobs, Tweedie); stubtest;
+- accessor values equal the corresponding `to_json()` fields;
+- a fresh digest equals the loaded digest, and both equal a recomputed digest;
+- writes to owned state arrays raise;
+- mismatched-data refusal still fires;
+- path evidence, candidates and checkpoint bytes are unchanged for a fixed seed.
